t even if that happens i think he'd  want to avoid any toxicity that might  come with this specific franchise  if i had to bet i'd say he either never  writes a new manga again  or if he does it will be something brand  new where you essentially start with the  clean slates  let me know in the comments if you agree  with that or not but if i'm right that  doesn't mean that attack on titan is  gone forever  much like the spinoffs that already  exists any future adaptation can be  written by someone who is not isayama  and this message in the final volume  makes it seem like at least they're not  ruling it out  the story still has potential for a  prequel or sequel that could be insanely  popular  and for the rest of the video i'm gonna  explain the top three options that would  get people excited  before we get into the top three ideas  for a sequel be sure to hit that sub  button as we are on the road to 400k  and drop a like as it does help out the  video  okay so the most interesting way to  continue attack on titan is to create a  spin-off manga set during the great  titan war  as this is by far the most fascinating  time in ld in history  back when elder conquered pretty much  the entire world the noble families then  began to fight each other in what willie  tiger described as an endless cycle of  conspiracy and betrayal  that premise alone sounds amazing as  each noble family would have had their  own distinct motivations depending on  which titan they had  those with the more powerful shifters  would want to maintain things the way  they are  whereas the family that had the kartisan  for example would likely have less  influence by comparison  a disparity of that nature could lead to  factions being created among the nobles  and you could have storylines where one  group bands together to try and steal  the titan of another  or where there's political disagreements  within a specific family over who's  going to inherit their titan  in my opinion if there was 