s  and focus on a previous generation of  warriors who had conflicting views about  whether they were doing the right thing  remember it took decades of  indoctrination for present-day aliens to  be as brainwashed as they are  but in the beginning a lot of them would  have been skeptical of the new malian  regime  i'm certain in the past you would have  found more people like zeke who were  pursuing their own agendas rather than  the agenda of mali  uh and perhaps along the way they tried  to convince other warriors to follow the  same path  that's why the current military now  checks if the warriors are still blindly  loyal before each mission  hence why they do these secret  evaluations finally the last idea that i  think would get people hyped is to do a  direct sequel to the event of the manga  but spoiler warning ahead as i will be  discussing the end of attack on titan  okay so back when the original final  chapter came out the last page was  mikasa thanking aaron  and those who watch my videos will know  that i thought it was mostly satisfying  i say that because things were left on  an open-ended note where there was room  to speculate what might happen next  and with armin going to initiate peace  talks things were relatively hopeful  i felt that conclusion was good since it  left certain things to our imagination  and while aaron's actions were  undeniably terrible there was still a  sense that what he did wasn't totally in  vain  however when the final volume came out  it added extra pages that for better or  worse completely reverse some of the big  consequences  and i guess the first one to mention  would be that parodies was destroyed  meaning that the peace talks that we saw  a few pages earlier were largely  meaningless  on top of that despite the power of the  titans disappearing it then reappears on  the new final page  and yeah i initially didn't know how to  feel about this because  i mean to be honest i thought it was  completely unnecessary but